proof.text:
Let $A$ be any nonempty small set. To apply condition (b) of [lem-coef-slice-cartesian-colimit-criterion] to an $A$-indexed coproduct cocone $q$, take any coproduct cocone $p$ and coherent transformation $\alpha:p	o q$; the cartesian condition on the discrete indexing set is automatic. Write $f_i=\alpha(i)$ and $f=\alpha(\infty)$. By [lem-coef-coherent-diagram-coyoneda] with $I=[1]$ and $\mathcal B=\mathcal E=\mathcal C$, $f$ is the coproduct of the $f_i$ in the arrow category. Fix $i\in A$ and let $f_{
e i}$ be the coproduct of the other arrows. The canonical decomposition $f\simeq f_i\amalg f_{
e i}$ follows from the coproduct mapping-space formula: a map out is exactly a map out of $f_i$ together with maps out of all other summands. Apply the cited criterion to the two-element coproduct of the targets of $f_i$ and $f_{
e i}$, and the transformation with these two arrows as components. Both source and target cocones are binary coproducts by the same pointwise assertion; step 3 gives condition (a). Hence condition (b) makes the leg $f_i	o f$ cartesian. This applies separately to every $i$, so condition (b) holds for the original $A$-coproduct. The criterion now gives condition (a) for that coproduct. Together with step 1 this proves that $ho$ preserves all small coproducts, including the empty one. The case $A=\{i\}$ uses the initial arrow for $f_{
e i}$ and is included.

